\newlabel{fig:cs137_longterm}{{4.5}{82}{Long-term evolution of $I_{\rm SC}$ under continuous $^{137}$Cs irradiation (44.16~rad\,hr$^{-1}$) over six days. The linear decline in $I_{\rm SC}$ with accumulated dose is attributed to a combination of radiation-induced defect creation in the perovskite absorber and progressive reduction in the optical transmittance of the glass superstrate~\cite {Boldyreva2020gammarad}}{figure.4.5}{}}
